BT 1 0 0 1 0 666 Tm /F1 14 Tf 20 TL (The organization was created with the goal of promoting international) Tj T* (cooperation and helping prevent another world war on the scale of the conflict) Tj T* (that had just ended. War Crimes and Justice The end of the war also raised) Tj T* (an important question: How should those responsible for major crimes during) Tj T* (the war be held accountable? The Allied powers established international and) Tj T* (national courts to prosecute people accused of serious wartime crimes. The) Tj T* (Nuremberg Trials became one of the most important examples. They helped) Tj T* (establish important principles concerning individual responsibility for crimes) Tj T* (committed during war and under government authority. The trials also) Tj T* (contributed to the development of international criminal law. The Lessons of) Tj T* (the War World War II left several major lessons for later generations. First,) Tj T* (international disagreements can become catastrophic when governments) Tj T* (choose aggression rather than peaceful solutions. Second, discrimination and) Tj T* (persecution can become increasingly dangerous when governments turn) Tj T* (prejudice into official policy. Third, civilians can suffer enormously during) Tj T* (modern warfare. Finally, rebuilding peace requires more than simply ending) Tj T* (fighting. Countries must also address displacement, economic destruction,) Tj T* (political instability, and the treatment of victims and survivors. World War II) Tj T* (therefore became not only a story of military campaigns, but also a major) Tj T* (turning point in the history of international relations and human rights. Key) Tj T* (Consequences of World War II Consequence Description Massive loss of life) Tj T* (An estimated 55 million people died worldwide Holocaust Six million) Tj T* (European Jews were murdered Displacement Millions of people were forced) Tj T* -0.041295 Tw (from their homes Destruction Cities, industries, transport systems, and homes) Tj T* 0 Tw (were devastated New world powers The United States and Soviet Union) Tj T* (emerged as dominant powers United Nations Founded in 1945 to promote) Tj T* (international cooperation Consequence Description Massive loss of life An) Tj T* (estimated 55 million people died worldwide Holocaust Six million European) Tj T* (Jews were murdered Displacement Millions of people were forced from their) Tj T* (homes Destruction Cities, industries, transport systems, and homes were) Tj T* (devastated New world powers The United States and Soviet Union emerged) Tj T* (as dominant powers United Nations Founded in 1945 to promote international) Tj T* (cooperation War-crimes trials Major perpetrators were prosecuted after the) Tj T* (war Cold War Rivalry between the US and Soviet Union shaped the postwar) Tj T* ET
